DESK-MEASURED DIAGNOSIS (verified today against the live signed-in seat profile, do not re-derive):
1. LATE RENDER is the primary cause. The Chat/Task control is a pair of `gem-segmented-button` custom elements (host data-value "0" = Chat, "40" = Task; each host contains one inner <button> whose text is exactly "Chat" / "Task"). The control is ABSENT from the DOM at 3 s and 8–10 s after navigation and appears at ~14 s (measured 13,996 ms in one run; 8–16 s headless, 10–25 s headed across runs). The model picker button (aria-label "Open mode picker, currently Hydrogen", text "Hydrogen") appears on the same late schedule. The current open() waits a fixed 3 s after domcontentloaded and ask calls readMode exactly once -> null -> gemini_task_mode_unavailable. Probe's model:null has the same root cause.
2. SELECTION-STATE BUG (latent, would break ask even with the wait fixed): the current readMode returns the innerText of the FIRST button matching /^(chat|task)$/i in DOM order — always "Chat", regardless of what is selected. Selection is actually carried by aria-pressed="true" on the selected segment's inner button AND the class "gem-segmented-button-selected" on its gem-segmented-button host (parent row style --gem-active-index flips 0 -> 1). Default selected mode on load is Chat.
3. DESK-VERIFIED INTERACTION: a real click on the Task segment's inner button selects Task (aria-pressed flips to true on Task, false on Chat; composer placeholder becomes "Describe a task"; task suggestions replace the chat greeting). No dropdown or mode picker step is involved. The current ask flow's click-"Chat"-first step is unnecessary; remove it.

IMPLEMENT in server/gemini_seat.mjs (ask command; keep probe/connect behavior and every named failure unchanged in spirit):
- Add a bounded wait helper: poll (every ~500 ms, up to 60 s) until the mode control exists in the DOM (gem-segmented-button elements, or buttons with exact text Chat/Task), then proceed; if it never appears, emit the existing named error gemini_task_mode_unavailable.
- In ask: after open() and the existing clickNewChat step (clicking New chat can re-render the shell, so the wait must come AFTER it), wait for the mode control as above.
- Replace readMode with selected-mode detection: return the text ('Chat' or 'Task') of the segment whose inner button has aria-pressed="true" (equivalently, whose host carries the gem-segmented-button-selected class); fall back to null when neither segment reports selected.
- If the selected mode is not Task: click the Task segment's inner button (a real element click on that button), then poll up to ~10 s until selected-mode detection returns 'Task'. If it never does, emit gemini_task_mode_unavailable. NEVER fill or submit the composer unless the verified selected mode is Task — the Task-mode-only guard is the owner's rule and stays absolute.
- After the wait, re-run detect() so the emitted result's model field reflects the late-rendered picker (Hydrogen) when present.
- Keep the response-collection loop and all other named errors (gemini_seat_not_signed_in, gemini_response_timeout, gemini_ask_failed) unchanged.

